# Mentions, not commands — read by tools/check-doc-verbs.sh (TODO 11.4a).
#
# A code span inside a sentence or a table cell is where prose and a command are
# STRUCTURALLY IDENTICAL: "`preserve.sh` two tiers" parses exactly like
# "`lab-fc.sh clone`". check-doc-verbs.sh refuses to guess between them, and is
# right to — but it then warned about the same nine rows on every run, and a
# warning list that never empties is one everybody learns to scroll past. This
# file is how a document says which it meant, once, with the reason.
#
# FORMAT:  <doc>  <tool-as-written>  <verb>   # why
#
# WHAT IT CANNOT DO: silence a fenced command. Only inline/table mentions consult
# this file; an instruction someone can copy out of a code block stays a hard
# failure whatever is written here, or this would be a way to bless a broken
# instruction.
#
# EVERY ENTRY IS RE-CHECKED, three ways, each a FAILURE:
#   * the document must still exist
#   * the tool must still NOT have the verb — if it gains one, the entry is
#     asserting a falsehood and the mention has become a real command
#   * it must silence something this run — an entry that matches nothing is
#     describing a sentence that has changed

# The micro-cloud plan's §8.1 table exists to say WHICH VERBS THE fc BACKEND DOES
# NOT HAVE, and why each absence is correct. Every cell here is the doc making
# exactly the point the checker would otherwise flag.
MICRO_CLOUD_LAB_PLAN.md   lab-fc.sh   console    # "no such verb. The fc backend was built without it and is right to have been"
MICRO_CLOUD_LAB_PLAN.md   lab-fc.sh   ssh        # "no such verb, and no plan to add one — the guest images run no sshd"
MICRO_CLOUD_LAB_PLAN.md   lab-fc.sh   preserve   # "not in this tool" — preserve is examples/micro-cloud/preserve.sh, one level up
MICRO_CLOUD_LAB_PLAN.md   lab-fc.sh   mmds       # "not a verb" — MMDS is a create-time key (--mmds / mmds = true)
MICRO_CLOUD_LAB_PLAN.md   lab-vm.sh   export     # struck through in the slice-7 row: the verb shipped as `export-tarball`
MICRO_CLOUD_LAB_PLAN.md   lab-vm.sh   boot       # prose in the slice-9 row ("...at first boot"), not an invocation

